  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Reproduce steps:\n1. Prepare nodes. Link them. Drop them to a Group.\n2. Hold CTRL key and click all nodes in the Group to select them all.\n3. Hold SHIFT key and drag one of selected nodes. The nodes go out from the Group and Group node shrinks. This is expected behavior, but also the Group node goes to the origin of axes.\n4. Select the Group node and try to drag it. The Group node isn't draggable now.\n5. Delete the Group node. Then edges disappear.\n6. Link nodes again. Then a Group appears. (!?) (This Group is draggable.)\n( Several strange behaviours exist in this operation sequence. IMO, disappearing edges is the most serious issue for users. So I chose it for the issue title. )",
